From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] refmvs: workaround MSVC 19.50/19.51 ARM64 miscompilation of
 add_spatial_candidate

Note: This is an AI Generated patch.

MSVC 19.50 (Visual Studio 18.0) miscompiles src/refmvs.c when targeting ARM64,
causing roughly half of dav1d's test cases to fail. Forcing the function to be
out-of-line avoids the bad inlining decision that triggers the codegen bug.

Reference: https://developercommunity.visualstudio.com/t/11032076

The fix only kicks in for MSVC on ARM64; every other compiler/target keeps
the original `static void` signature, so there is no perf impact elsewhere.
---
 src/refmvs.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/refmvs.c b/src/refmvs.c
--- a/src/refmvs.c
+++ b/src/refmvs.c
@@ -38,7 +38,14 @@
 #include "src/mem.h"
 #include "src/refmvs.h"
 
-static void add_spatial_candidate(refmvs_candidate *const mvstack, int *const cnt,
+#if defined(_MSC_VER) && defined(_M_ARM64)
+/* Workaround for MSVC 19.50/19.51 ARM64 miscompilation, see
+ * https://developercommunity.visualstudio.com/t/11032076 */
+#define DAV1D_REFMVS_NOINLINE __declspec(noinline)
+#else
+#define DAV1D_REFMVS_NOINLINE
+#endif
+static DAV1D_REFMVS_NOINLINE void add_spatial_candidate(refmvs_candidate *const mvstack, int *const cnt,
                                   const int weight, const refmvs_block *const b,
                                   const union refmvs_refpair ref, const mv gmv[2],
                                   int *const have_newmv_match,
